Z||000000||jhstokes||03-23-2000||09:38 PM||||I own an 88 GT V6 5speed. I would like to do a Northstar conversion. Does anyone have any info on links,conversion kits, cost , etc ???||||reg||5
Z||000001||frontal lobe||03-23-2000||11:57 PM||||Welcome to the forum!  Check out <A HREF="http://www.designonesystems.com." TARGET=_blank>www.designonesystems.com.</A>   They have a northstar conversion kit.  I don't know anything about quality, degree of difficulty, etc.  They quote a ballpark price of conversion kit and engine of 7500 to 9000!!!!  They figure 4500 for their kit and 3000 to 4500 for the engine.  You should be able to get off cheaper with a small block chevy conversion with the same or more horsepower, but you may just love the sound and weight of the northstar.  Either way, glad to know we are getting some independently wealthy people on the forum!!!  Just joking!  Just jealous.  I've got the fiero and an lt1 and am getting close to doing the swap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan86gt3.8||03-24-2000||12:02 AM||||why sure links are <A HREF="http://www.americancustom.eng" TARGET=_blank>www.americancustom.eng</A>  (where I got the kit for my engine convrsion).  Its american custom engineering and he is in Durango, CO. but he only does northstars in house.  The only other place I know of is design one in oklahoma city, OK.  they are at <A HREF="http://www.designonesystems.com/." TARGET=_blank>http://www.designonesystems.com/.</A> <BR>As for the price I think design one says like 7-9k and I am not sure on ace, but prices are there for booth.  There is also a guy who did a conversion himself and put a 125 shot on it, he has ben in kit car, hot rod, and gm highperformance.  His name is John Norman.  Thats all I can think of right now!  Hey let me know if its feisable for you and if you are going to do it or not!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||03-24-2000||12:17 AM||||The last time I was at Ed Rosey Park's Fiero Factory near Huntsville Alabama ((256) 420-5391  Fierofactory@juno.com) he had a Northstar already mounted in a cradle that he was selling for a customer who changed his mind.  It had the axels and everything.  I believe the price was around $5000 or so.  That was in July 99.||||reg||1
Z||000004||jhogans||03-24-2000||11:47 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.design1Systems.com" TARGET=_blank>www.design1Systems.com</A>  quoted me of a turnkey install for $15000.  From what I can remember, they were the first to put a Northstar in a Fiero.  They were also featured in Kit Car magazine.  They are also working on a Twin Turbo for the Northstar.  They expect to get 400HP+.  But expect to pay an extra $6000.<P>The thing is, you will need to use the Automatic Northstar transmission.  I have a 5speed also and I considered this swap but I do love the manual transmission.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||jhogans||03-24-2000||11:48 AM||||BTW,  Ed Parks doesn't have the Northstar engine any longer.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Richard Parnell||03-24-2000||01:19 PM||||Some of the prices quoted for V8 conversions really amaze me.  I plan on using V8 Archies master kit ($3250) I could kick myself for not buying it several years ago but that's another story.  I bought a good running Chevy Caprice with a rebuilt 350 w/towing cam for $450 and pulled the engine. That's a total of $3700 and I figure maybe another $500 to complete the conversion. I'm doing the work myself with a friend helping (he's going to open the beers)<BR>But then there's the cost of suspension changes I want/need to do.  So I figure another $2-3000 for that.  Then I want to repaint.  Still for less than $8000 I will have ensentially a nicer faster car than I could buy for $20-30000. ||||reg||6
Z||000007||Dan86gt3.8||03-24-2000||04:54 PM||||Hell yes!  Thats what I am saying, if northstar, ls1 or lt1, or turbo 3.8 in my car its gona be running with the new fbody's.  Northstar is expensve but well worth it, as would be a gn motor or turbo series II. just my $.02.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||03-24-2000||06:24 PM||||Anybody considered putting a flat-4 out of an older VW Beetle in their Fiero??  I'll bet you could do it cheaper than a Northstar.  (And the sound.  Aaahhhhhh...)||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||03-24-2000||07:55 PM||||Just think.....no more cooling system problems.  Heck, no more cooling system!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>You would definitely need to figure out a good way to get enough airflow inside the engine compartment, but that shouldn't be a big deal.  <P>I can imagine a base coupe with a 1776 (or bigger) Bug engine all dressed up.  What a hoot that would be!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000010||lowCG||03-25-2000||02:00 AM||||I knew this guy back in high school who had a built bug motor in a Fiat X-19.Was pretty darned fast too,painted black,had big Webers on it,and the transaxle almost stuck out of the rear of the car,and was polished.<BR>How about a Northstar onto a Chrysler tranny?<BR>That way you could shift like the F1 drivers do,and have a longitudinal mounting.Would probably have to add about seven inches to the frame/wheelbase though.||||reg||1
